   "evidence": "In the lemma body, `w'` is built from `(lp.mem\u2113p w).indicator_comp hinj` with the norm bound `lp.norm_le_of_forall_eq_indicator_comp hp hinj`, and `hw'` shows `w' i = shiftRight M w i`. The rest is `lp.exists_eq_tsum_smul_add_and_norm_le hgeom w'` plus `tsum_geometric_of_lt_one`. The only call site is `Reconstruction.lean`: `obtain \u27e8y, hy, hy_norm\u27e9 := lp.exists_hasSum_geometric_shiftRight hr L w`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Normed/Lp/Reindex.lean",
   "fix": "Expose the shift fact as its own lemma, e.g. `lp.shiftRight (M) (w : lp (fun _ \u21a6 E) p) : lp (fun _ \u21a6 E) p` with `coeFn = shiftRight M w` and `\u2016lp.shiftRight M w\u2016 \u2264 \u2016w\u2016` (or `Mem\u2113p.shiftRight` plus the norm bound). In the Besov proof, apply `lp.exists_eq_tsum_smul_add_and_norm_le` to it directly with the kernel `\u03c1\u207b\u00b9 ^ m` and drop `lp.exists_hasSum_geometric_shiftRight`.",
   "issue": "`lp.exists_hasSum_geometric_shiftRight` combines two things: the generic fact that `shiftRight M w` is in \u2113\u1d56 with norm at most \u2016w\u2016 (proved privately as the local `w'`), and a geometric kernel `r\u1d50` that only `Reconstruction.lean:136` uses. The reusable shift fact is not exposed, and the kernel-specific statement adds a needless `NormedDivisionRing` lemma to a general \u2113\u1d56 file.",
   "line": 161
  }
